            "review_title": "Review at Food Exchange Saigon South",
            "review_text": "Anh Amắn 🇻🇳\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam12939 contributions\n46\nExcellent Seafood Buffet\nJan 2025 • Friends\nI booked a Friday night Seafood Buffet dinner for my partner and two of our close friends. \n\nOur table was a lovely window seat and once we were all seated and had ordered a bottle of Australian Chardonnay and a couple of soft drinks we explored the buffet selection. \n\nThere were lots of salads and cooked side dishes, a good mix of both seafood and non seafood to choose from. The seafood dishes included cooked tiger prawns, sea snails, a cooked fish dish, seafood soup & sushi. There was also a large, very fresh seafood station that included fresh oysters, crabs, squid, giant prawns and clams. These you could have steamed or grilled or cooked to order in various sauces like Singapore or Tamarind or Black Pepper sauce. The oysters were available, natural, or prepared to order with cheese or another fresh style. There were also a large variety of seafood sauces to select from for dipping.\n\nThe food was simply delicious and we ate to our hearts and stomachs contentment. For dessert there was a selection ranging from Vietnamese desserts to tropical fruit, to chocolate and cheese cake and strawberry yogurt and a selection of 5 different ice creams. \n\nThe service was truly excellent and we felt taken care of by the staff. We left the restaurant totally happy and full. We would definitely think of dinning here again for their Seafood Buffet.\nRead more\nWritten January 18, 2025",
